An interdisciplinary AI researcher and postdoctoral scientist with a PhD in mechanical engineering, specializing in Neuro-Symbolic AI, machine learning, and advanced manufacturing. With an extensive publication record spanning high-impact journals and international conferences, I bridge the gap between complex physical systems and algorithmic innovation. Beyond research, I am deeply committed to institutional advancement by serving on EDI and Data Management committees, deploying open-science data repositories, and modernizing university curricula for big data processing. My aim is to continue driving forward institutional research capabilities while mentoring the next generation of data-driven scientists.